window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226 The Blanket","paragraphs":["\"Why are all my photos stored back here?\" Eira asked.","Gwen glanced up from the box. \"That photographer, Lainey, said she was making a documentary. She’s been asking about children who grew up here and went on to do something with their lives.\"","She gave Eira a small smile.","\"You’re the biggest success story we have. But you asked me to keep your information private, so I put everything away. I didn’t want her digging through your records or catching anything on camera.\"","A chill brushed the back of Eira’s neck.","It sounded as if Lainey had been asking about her.","Then again, a documentary covered people as well as places. Lainey’s questions were not suspicious on the surface.","\"What has she been doing since she arrived?\" Eira asked.","\"Mostly talking to people around the orphanage. She says she’s collecting stories for the film.\" Gwen frowned. \"To be honest, it feels less like a fundraising video and more like she’s looking for something.\"","\"What kind of something?\"","\"Nothing specific enough to make me stop her. If she had crossed a line, someone would’ve come to me.\"","Eira nodded, though the answer did little to ease her mind.","She turned back to the storage box and lifted a stack of old photographs. Beneath them, she found a small bundle sealed in a clear plastic bag.","Inside was a piece of blue-striped cotton.","Eira frowned. \"What is this?\"","Gwen went still.","\"That’s the blanket you were wrapped in when they found you.\"","Eira looked up. \"Mine?\"","Gwen nodded.","Every child brought to the orphanage had their clothes washed, labeled, and stored. Most of those items were ordinary. This one was not.","Eira opened the bag carefully.","The cotton was soft with age. Tiny airplanes had been stitched between the blue stripes.","\"That was expensive fabric back then,\" Gwen said quietly. \"High-end baby clothes. We thought your family might have lost you by accident instead of leaving you behind.\"","Eira ran her thumb over one of the faded airplanes.","\"We spent fifteen days checking with every neighboring Pack along the border,\" Gwen continued. \"We asked about missing pups, searched the shelters, and contacted the regional records office. Nothing came up.\"","She hesitated.","\"There was one strange detail. The blanket was made for a boy.\"","Eira’s head snapped up. \"A boy?\"","\"The pattern, the size, even the way it was sewn. Everything suggested it had been bought for a male pup.\"","Gwen lowered herself into the old office chair.","\"You know the rest. You grew up here, worked harder than anyone, and built a life far beyond this town. You never forgot the Omega House either. You’ve been giving back ever since you had the means.\"","Eira set the blanket down and wrapped her arms around Gwen.","\"Thank you,\" she whispered. \"For taking me in. For giving me a home.\"","Gwen patted her back.","\"All right. Don’t make me cry before breakfast.\"","Eira pulled away, smiling through the tightness in her throat.","Gwen’s expression softened. \"Do you want to look for your family?\"","Eira glanced at the storage box.","\"We kept the paper records. There isn’t much, but it’s a place to start.\"","Eira pressed her lips together.","\"If the answers are there, I’ll find them.\"","That was not quite an answer, and Gwen knew it.","\"If I was left on purpose, then there’s nothing to chase,\" Eira said. \"But if I was lost, my family may still be looking for me.\"","She folded the blanket back into the plastic bag.","\"I just need to give them a reason to find me.\"","Gwen reached for her hand. \"You don’t have to prove that you’re worth finding.\"","\"I know.\"","But knowing that and believing her family would find her were two different things.","People searched for what they remembered. If her family had lost a little boy, they might never think to look for the woman she had become.","Eira glanced toward the dining hall, where Lainey was still filming the children.","Lainey was the only person who had recently gone out of her way to learn about Eira’s past.","--","In Palo Alto, Alpha Killian took a screenshot of the address Eira had sent him and forwarded it to Lila without saying a word.","A voice message came back almost at once.","\"You’re so immature.\"","\"You’re the immature one!\"","Alpha Killian ignored the rest of her rant.","His flight landed a short time later. Natalie had arranged a driver, but Alpha Killian waved him off and took the wheel himself.","While he drove, he sent Eira his itinerary. She was already reviewing the information Gwen had given her about Sam, including possible routes, places to stay, and transportation options.","Eira could handle rough conditions. She had traveled alone before and knew how to take care of herself.","She was only worried about Alpha Killian.","After sending Alpha Killian the details, Eira questioned the longtime staff.","The gatekeeper, kitchen staff, and dorm supervisors gave her the same answer. Lainey had asked about the orphanage’s history and whether any former residents had gone on to become successful or appeared in the news.","Most had told her little. One of the nursery workers pulled Eira aside.","\"I mentioned you,\" she admitted. \"Miss Gwen showed me an article about your work and asked me to read it to the kids. One of them recognized you as Big Sister Eira, so I told Lainey you grew up here and now work in Palo Alto.\"","\"When?\"","\"Three days ago.\"","\"Did she ask anything else?\"","\"Not really. She thanked me and went back to playing with the children. They adore her.\"","That answer should have reassured Eira. Instead, it left her with more questions.","Eira thanked the woman and stepped back into the hallway.","\"Oh, and she was asking about the old records earlier,\" the woman added. \"I saw her heading toward the archive room.\"","Eira stopped. \"The records room?\"","\"She said she wanted some background for the documentary. I didn’t think much of it.\"","Eira thanked her and headed down the hall.","The archive door stood partly open. Inside, Lainey was filming the faded photographs and rows of filing cabinets. When she heard Eira approach, she lowered the camera and turned with a pleasant smile.","\"Eira. I was just looking for you.\"","\"Were you?\"","Lainey’s smile stayed in place, but her grip tightened around the camera.","\"I wanted footage of the older part of the building. It has character.\"","\"The records room?\"","\"I was curious.\"","\"Can I see what you filmed?\"","Lainey studied her for a moment, then handed over the camera.","\"Sure.\"","Eira skimmed the footage. It showed the grounds, the children, and a few old photographs. Nothing private or obviously invasive.","She returned the camera.","\"You’ve asked a lot about the orphanage’s history,\" Eira said. \"You also wanted to know whether any former residents became successful.\"","Lainey blinked once, then recovered.","\"History gives the documentary a stronger story. A successful former resident gives people someone to connect with. It’s good publicity.\"","\"Someone told you about me.\"","Lainey gave a small nod. \"Someone did.\"","\"If you plan to use my name or image, get permission first. The last outlet that interviewed me was a national news organization. My work involves federal security clearance, so people take the handling of my information seriously.\"","Lainey’s smile froze before smoothly returning.","\"Thanks for the warning. I wouldn’t dream of crossing a line.\"","\"Good luck with the shoot.\"","Eira turned and walked away.","The moment she disappeared around the corner, Lainey’s smile vanished. She had come to this remote stretch of Pack territory looking for something useful. Most of the staff had kept quiet, but she had finally learned that Eira had grown up there.","Then Eira had shown up and shut down the conversation.","Wasn’t she supposed to be busy dealing with Serena and the lawsuit?","Lainey pulled out her phone and called Serena.","She needed to know what had changed."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227 The Substitute","paragraphs":["Lainey slipped into a quiet corner of the courtyard and called Serena.","After a few polite words, she lowered her voice.","\"I’m out in the border territory filming. Guess who showed up?\"","Serena went quiet.","\"Eira,\" Lainey said. \"She’s back at the Omega House, nowhere near Palo Alto. That means she can’t keep an eye on you and Sebastian. You two get a little more breathing room.\"","Lainey had a talent for making every suggestion sound like a favor. She never pushed outright. She simply offered a tempting detail, then waited for someone to reach for it.","Serena took the bait.","\"Eira went back to the Omega House?\"","So that was why Alpha Sebastian had said Eira probably would not move forward with the lawsuit anytime soon.","\"Is something wrong?\" Lainey asked, her voice full of concern.","\"Something came up,\" Serena said. \"She was pressuring us hard, then suddenly backed off. She must have something more important to deal with.\"","\"Well, at least she’s off your back for now. As long as you’re okay.\"","\"Thanks, Lainey.\"","\"Of course.\" Lainey let a few seconds pass before adding, \"Still, what could be so important that she’d fly all the way out to the border?\"","Serena hesitated. \"I don’t know.\"","Lainey’s fingers tightened around her phone.","Was Eira looking for her birth family? Had someone finally uncovered a lead?","Her pulse quickened. The elevation was already making her chest feel tight.","Lainey’s body had never handled the mountain air well.She forced herself to breathe slowly.","\"Sorry,\" she said. \"I’m losing signal out here. I need to go.\"","Before Serena could ask another question, Lainey ended the call.","--","Meanwhile, Eira waited near the main entrance of the Omega House for Alpha Killian.","Her phone rang. Lila was calling.","\"Is my brother there yet?\"","\"Not yet.\" Eira glanced toward the gate. Cars passed along the highway, but none turned into the driveway.","\"So what did you bribe him with?\"","\"Eight hundred a day.\"","Lila went quiet for a second.","Then Eira heard her choke on her drink.","\"Hold on. Sorry.\" Lila coughed, then started laughing. \"Eight hundred? That’s not even a serious consulting fee for a man like my brother.\"","\"It was his number.\"","\"Please. Killian doesn’t need eight hundred dollars. He probably spends more than that on coffee.\"","Eira glanced toward the empty driveway. \"Are you done?\"","\"Not even close. With his face and that body, he could charge a fortune for a private appearance.\"","\"Lila.\"","\"What? I’m being supportive.\"","\"You’re being ridiculous.\"","\"I’m being honest. If he walked into one of those celebrity charity events, someone would pay ten grand just to have him stand next to their table.\"","Eira had no idea how to respond to that.","A car horn sounded near the gate.","She turned as a black Rolls-Royce Cullinan rolled onto the property.","Alpha Killian stepped out, tall and composed in a dark wool coat. The guard straightened before waving him through.","\"I have to go,\" Eira said.","\"What? Why?\"","\"The escort is here.\"","Lila burst out laughing.","Eira ended the call before Lila could say anything worse and hurried toward the car.","\"He’s with me,\" she told the guard.","Alpha Killian closed the driver’s door and walked toward her. The wind caught Eira’s hair and blew it across her face. She pushed it behind her ears, but the cold had already turned the tip of her nose pink.","Alpha Killian frowned and stepped in front of her, blocking the wind with his body.","\"You should have worn a hat.\"","\"I forgot.\"","\"You forgot a hat in the middle of winter?\"","\"I had other things to worry about.\" She looked toward the main building. \"Come on. Gwen wants me to bring someone I trust before I follow Sam’s lead.\"","\"Then let’s go.\"","\"You’re not tired?\"","\"No.\"","They started toward the building.","Eira lowered her voice. \"Lainey is here.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression cooled.","\"Then watch what you say.\"","\"Because of our cover?\"","\"The married-couple story.\"","Eira glanced up at him. \"Does the package include a warranty?\"","Alpha Killian looked down at her.","She had no idea where she had picked up that phrase, and he decided not to ask.","\"Yes,\" he said. \"It does.\"","For eight hundred dollars a day, Eira thought, that seemed fair.","Alpha Killian had wanted to inspect the property before they left. The Omega House sat near the edge of Pack territory, where city services were limited and patrol routes mattered. He wanted to see the security system, the fence line, and how the border Pack protected the children.","Eira was already pulling him toward Gwen’s office.","He knew Gwen’s background. She was fifty-one, had received a regional service award, and had run the Omega House for most of Eira’s life.","She was not just the director.","She was Eira’s family.","Eira knocked once and opened the door.","\"Miss Gwen, he’s here.\" She stepped aside. \"This is Killian Sterling.\"","Gwen stood and reached for her reading glasses.","\"Mr. Sterling.\"","\"Killian is fine.\" He shook her hand. \"Eira calls me that.\"","Gwen studied him for a moment. He was young, powerful, and clearly accustomed to being obeyed. Still, he had come all the way out here because Eira had asked.","That counted for something.","\"You’re prepared to protect her?\"","Alpha Killian took a business card from his wallet and set it on the desk.","\"If anything happens, call that number. If Eira is hurt because of me, the Sterling family will take responsibility.\"","His voice was quiet, but there was nothing casual about the promise.","Gwen picked up the card and looked at him more carefully.","\"Thank you,\" she said.","Alpha Killian nodded.","Gwen had seen men promise to take care of Eira before. Most of them had offered words and nothing else. Alpha Killian had come with a plan, transportation, and a way to reach him directly.","She walked them outside.","\"The county is rougher than Palo Alto,\" she warned Eira. \"Stay together, keep your phones charged, and call me if anything feels wrong.\"","\"I will.\"","They were almost at the gate when Lainey stepped out of the dining hall with her camera hanging from one shoulder.","\"Killian,\" Lainey called, bright and friendly. \"What brings you all the way out here?\"","He kept walking.","\"Not your concern.\"","Her smile tightened, but she turned to Eira instead.","\"You two seem pretty close.\"","\"Glad you can tell,\" Alpha Killian said without looking back.","A flicker of annoyance crossed Lainey’s face.","\"So where are you headed now?\"","\"Back to Palo Alto,\" Eira said.","\"Already? You just got here.\"","Before the question could turn into an interrogation, Gwen stepped in.","\"That was my doing,\" she said easily. \"I asked Eira to come back because something urgent came up. It’s taken care of now, so she needs to get going.\"","Lainey’s eyes moved from Gwen to Eira, then settled on Alpha Killian.","Urgent.","So Alpha Killian was covering for Eira. And now Gwen was covering for her too.","Lainey gave a small nod, as if she accepted the explanation.","\"Of course,\" she said. \"I hope everything worked out.\"","\"Thanks,\" Eira replied.","Lainey’s smile stayed polite, but her mind was already working.","Whatever had brought Eira here, it was more important than Lainey had expected."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228 The Search Begins","paragraphs":["The moment the SUV pulled away from the Omega House, Eira opened her tablet and pulled up the plan she had prepared earlier.","\"It’s four forty,\" she said. \"We’ll reach the county line around five thirty. We’ll grab dinner first, then check the neighborhood where Sam’s uncle used to live. Between seven and eight, people should be home and willing to talk.\"","Alpha Killian kept one hand on the wheel. His other rested near the gearshift, relaxed but ready. He glanced at her tablet, then at the focused crease between her brows.","\"After that, we can check the three high schools in the county. They all sit along the same main road, so we can cover them quickly. If we don’t find anything tonight, we start again in the morning. Then we get a hotel.\"","Eira finally looked up. \"Does that work for you?\"","\"You’re in charge.\"","\"That sounds suspiciously like you’re trying to avoid responsibility.\"","\"I’m the hired help.\" His mouth twitched. \"Eight hundred dollars a day. I follow orders.\"","The number reminded her of Lila’s ridiculous comments about Alpha Killian’s private appearance fee.","\"Killian.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"Eight hundred is not enough.\"","His silver-gray eyes slid toward her. \"Then name your price.\"","Eira hesitated. \"A thousand?\"","\"Fine.\"","He said it so easily that she narrowed her eyes. \"You didn’t even negotiate.\"","\"You were worried about underpaying me.\"","\"I was being fair.\"","\"I know.\"","The warmth in his voice made her look back at the tablet.","They reached the diner five minutes ahead of schedule. The small roadside place was bright and crowded, its windows fogged from the cold. The smell of coffee, fried onions, and warm pie filled the air.","When Alpha Killian walked in wearing a tailored coat, several heads turned. A woman at the counter whispered something to her friend, who glanced over and nearly spilled her coffee.","Eira led him to a corner booth before anyone could come over.","They ordered grilled chicken, soup, fries, and coffee. Eira chose the cheapest items on the menu, but Alpha Killian noticed.","\"Don’t worry about the bill,\" he said quietly.","\"I’m not.\"","\"You are.\"","She looked up from her menu.","\"We’re here to find Sam,\" Alpha Killian continued. \"Eat something warm. Get a decent room. Stop apologizing for taking care of yourself.\"","The words settled somewhere deep in her chest.","She closed the menu. \"Fine. But I’m still paying your fee.\"","\"I’ll send an invoice.\"","\"You’d better.\"","After dinner, they drove to the neighborhood where Sam’s uncle had lived.","The street sat beyond the county’s better-maintained roads. Puddles filled the cracked pavement, old trash cans leaned beside narrow porches, and damp smoke drifted from backyard fire pits.","A few children in puffy winter coats raced between the buildings while their parents called after them.","They had barely reached the first row of apartments when people began watching them.","A man sitting on a porch glanced at the photo on Eira’s phone and muttered, \"Wonder if they’re here about Nate.\"","Eira caught the name and approached a group of older women gathered beneath an awning.","\"Evening. Sorry to bother you. Did a man named Jordan come around here recently?\"","She showed them the photo.","One woman nodded. \"I’ve seen him. He came looking for Nate. After that, Nate told everyone the family was getting a fresh start somewhere up north.\"","\"Did he say where?\"","\"No,\" another woman said. \"He kept that part to himself.\"","\"Are you family?\" someone asked.","\"I’m Sam’s sister.\"","The women’s expressions softened.","\"You’re the girl from the Omega House,\" one of them said. \"Sam’s sister. Sweet boy.\"","\"Nate called him the family’s good-luck charm,\" another added. \"Said Sam would bring them better luck wherever they went.\"","\"Good-luck charm, my ass.\" A third woman snorted. \"That boy hauled trash, watched the little kids, and got slapped whenever they cried. Nate treated him like free labor.\"","Eira’s jaw tightened.","Then one woman lowered her voice. \"Nate used to brag about getting SSI for Sam. Said the boy brought in a few hundred dollars a month.\"","\"SSI for what?\" someone asked.","\"Autism, I think. And Nate claimed Sam was missing a thumb too.\"","Eira went still.","\"What?\"","Sam had left the Omega House with both hands intact. Eira had helped him dress. She knew exactly what she had seen.","Eira drew in a slow breath, then looked back at the women.","\"Did Nate mention where they were taking Sam?\"","The women exchanged glances.","\"Some kind of school,\" one said. \"A place for kids who need extra help.\"","\"A special school?\" another asked. \"There isn’t one in this county.\"","\"That’s still helpful,\" Eira said.","She pulled a business card from her wallet and handed it to the oldest woman.","\"If you remember anything else, please call me. Any time.\"","The woman studied the card. \"You really looking for that boy?\"","\"He’s my brother.\"","The woman’s expression softened. \"Then I hope you find him.\"","Eira thanked them and led Alpha Killian back toward the SUV.","Alpha Killian glanced at her. \"What do we know?\"","He couldn’t make out every word through the women’s overlapping voices and rapid-fire local expressions. But he saw Eira’s face change, and that told him enough.","\"Beta Jordan came looking for Nate. Nate moved the family north, claimed Sam was receiving SSI, and told people the boy was missing a thumb.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","\"Which isn’t true,\" Eira said. \"Sam left the Omega House with both hands intact.\"","She searched the nearby school districts on her phone.","\"The woman may have meant a special education program, not a separate school. There’s a nonpublic school in the next county, but we need to verify it.\"","\"Can we go tonight?\"","\"The schools are closed. And they can’t release Sam’s records without legal authorization.\"","\"Then I’ll make the calls.\"","While Eira checked district websites, Alpha Killian contacted his attorney. A few minutes later, Miles sent an update.","Miles: The county registrar can meet with you at eight tomorrow morning. They’ll verify whether Sam’s name appears in recent transfers, but they can’t release protected records without authorization.","Eira glanced at Alpha Killian. \"That was fast.\"","\"Money buys speed. Not access.\"","She almost smiled. \"You sound responsible.\"","\"I have my moments.\"","Eira opened the website for the specialized school. Its polished pages were full of bright photos and vague testimonials. There were no parent complaints, angry reviews, or local discussions.","That did not prove anything. Small private schools often had little online presence.","Still, the site looked too clean.","\"It’s our best lead,\" she said.","\"We’ll check it in the morning.\"","They returned to the SUV. Eira climbed into the passenger seat and kept scrolling through the school’s website.","\"Give me a minute,\" Alpha Killian said.","Before she could ask where he was going, he crossed the road to a taco truck closing beneath a string of yellow lights.","He returned with two paper bags and two cups of hot chocolate.","\"Chicken tacos,\" he said, handing her one bag. \"And churros.\"","Eira wrapped her hands around the warm cup. \"You got both?\"","\"Something spicy and something sweet.\"","The smell of grilled meat, lime, and cinnamon drifted through the cold air.","\"You went through all that trouble for tacos?\"","\"You were hungry.\"","\"I never said I was.\"","\"You didn’t have to.\"","Their fingers brushed as she took the bags.","\"Thank you.\"","After the tacos, they found a decent hotel near the highway.","The place was small but clean, with warm lighting, dark wood floors, and a front desk decorated with winter wreaths. Alpha Killian handed over his ID. Eira placed hers beside it.","\"The reservation is under my name,\" she told the clerk.","The clerk checked the screen. \"Two deluxe king rooms. Next door to each other?\"","\"That works.\"","A few minutes later, they reached the second floor.","Alpha Killian stopped outside his door. \"Get some sleep. Tomorrow is the important day.\"","\"I will.\"","She entered her room and closed the door.","A few seconds later, his door clicked shut next to hers."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229 The Boy in the Ambulance","paragraphs":["Morning came gray and bitterly cold.","After washing up, Eira knocked on Alpha Killian ’s door. He opened it almost immediately. Faint shadows sat beneath his silver-gray eyes.","The hotel mattress had been too soft, the walls too thin, and freight trucks had rumbled along the highway most of the night. Alpha Killian looked as composed as ever.","\"Breakfast here or on the road?\" he asked.","\"On the road.\"","They met the county education liaison in the lobby. He was waiting beside a county-issued sedan with a folder tucked beneath one arm.","\"The registrar is ready for you,\" he said. \"We’ll start there. If the district finds a possible match, I’ll contact the school and arrange a meeting.\"","Eira stopped at the café near the front desk and bought three breakfast bags: sausage, egg, and cheese biscuits, hash browns, coffee, and bottled orange juice.","She could eat while they drove. Alpha Killian needed both hands on the wheel, and he had barely slept. She made a mental note to get her license as soon as possible.","Forty minutes later, they pulled into the county education office.","The registrar checked Eira’s identification and reviewed the documents Gwen had provided to confirm her connection to Sam.","\"I need to be clear about what I can and can’t do,\" she said. \"I can’t show you protected student records. But I can search recent transfers using Sam’s legal name, age, and date of birth. If I find a possible match, I can contact the receiving school and ask them to verify the student’s safety.\"","\"And if his name was changed?\" Eira asked.","\"Then the search may come back empty. If this involves an endangered child, law enforcement or a court order can request more information.\"","Eira tightened her hand around her phone.","The registrar made several calls. She asked about recent transfers, private placements, and residential programs in the neighboring district. Ten minutes later, she put down the phone.","\"There’s a private residential program in the neighboring district that recently admitted a boy who matches Sam’s age and support needs. The student is registered under a different name. It’s only a possible match, but it’s the closest lead I found.\"","Eira’s breath caught. \"Can you tell me what name they used?\"","\"I’m sorry. Not without proper authorization.\" The registrar glanced at the liaison. \"But I can ask the school administrator to meet with you. The county office can verify the inquiry without releasing the student’s file.\"","It was not enough, but it was a lead.","They left the office and climbed into their vehicles. The liaison’s sedan pulled onto the highway, and Alpha Killian followed.","Half an hour into the drive, Eira opened one of the breakfast bags.","\"You need to eat.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","\"You look exhausted.\"","\"I’m driving.\"","\"That’s not an answer.\"","She unwrapped a sausage biscuit and held it out. Alpha Killian kept his eyes on the road, but after a moment, he leaned over and took it from her fingers.","Her fingertip brushed his lower lip.","His skin felt dry from the cold.","Eira quickly steadied the biscuit before it fell apart. \"I wiped my hands. It’s clean. You’ll survive one breakfast sandwich.\"","Alpha Killian gave her a sideways glance.","\"If you hate it, I’ll make you something better when we get home.\"","He finished the biscuit in two bites. Eira lifted the straw from the orange juice and held it out. He took a drink without complaint, then returned his attention to the road.","\"Make me breakfast sandwiches bigger than your fist,\" he said.","Eira blinked.","Then she remembered the homemade dishes she used to bring to Sterling Group. Everyone on the executive floor had received some except Alpha Killian .He had not forgotten.","A small smile tugged at her lips. \"You’re still holding a grudge?\"","\"I remember what matters.\"","The warmth in his voice eased something tight in her chest.","The county sedan eventually turned off the highway onto a private road. A sign marked the entrance to a residential program for students with intensive support needs.","A security guard stepped out of the gatehouse. The liaison lowered his window, showed his county identification, and explained the registrar’s request.","The guard made a quick call, then opened the gate.","Inside, the campus was quiet and carefully maintained. A landscaped pond divided the main drive. The academic buildings stood to the right, while the residential wing sat behind a line of tall cedar trees on the left.","The vehicles turned toward the academic buildings.","They had gone less than a hundred yards when an ambulance siren cut through the morning.","Eira looked in the side mirror.","An ambulance came from the residential wing with its lights flashing. It sped past the gatehouse and disappeared onto the highway.","She could not see who was inside.","The road curved, blocking her view, but a cold weight had already settled in her chest.","The liaison parked near the main entrance and led them inside.","The building was clean and well maintained, but the halls were loud. Voices echoed behind closed doors. A student shouted from one classroom while a staff member repeated the same calm instruction.","\"Residential programs can be intense,\" the liaison said carefully. \"The students have different support needs. Some are quiet. Some need constant supervision. A few may become aggressive when they’re overwhelmed.\"","Alpha Killian turned his head and gave him a hard look.","The liaison stopped talking.","They reached the administration office. Before he could knock, a man in a staff polo opened the door. He recognized the county liaison and forced a polite smile.","\"Good morning.\"","\"This is Mr. Sterling, and this is Ms. Crawford,\" the liaison said. \"The registrar asked us to follow up on a possible transfer.\"","The staff member’s smile faded when he saw Eira’s phone.","She held up Sam’s photograph.","\"This is my brother. His name is Sam.\"","The color drained from the man’s face.","Alpha Killian ’s voice turned cold. \"Where is he?\"","\"Everything is under control,\" the staff member said too quickly.","A principal stepped out from behind a desk. He looked calmer than the others, but sweat darkened the collar of his shirt.","\"The student is registered here as Jae,\" he said. \"J-A-E.\"","Eira’s brow tightened.","The principal glanced at the staff member.","\"Jae is autistic,\" the man said. \"He is mostly nonverbal and needs close supervision. He likes to climb. Trees, stairwells, fences. We have staff assigned to monitor him.\"","\"Then how did he get out of a second-floor window?\" Alpha Killian asked.","The man swallowed.","\"We found him outside the residential wing early this morning. He had fallen from a window. We called emergency services right away.\"","\"Why are you saying it like you’re not sure?\" Eira asked.","\"We are sure,\" the principal cut in. \"The fall was from the second floor. The ambulance crew took him to County General.\"","Eira’s stomach dropped.","The ambulance at the gate. The flashing lights. The residential wing.","Sam had been inside it.","Her hands turned cold. \"When did this happen?\"","\"Just after dawn.\"","\"And you waited until now to tell anyone?\"","No one argued.","Eira was already running toward the SUV.","They reached County General less than twenty minutes later.","Alpha Killian stopped at the emergency entrance, and Eira jumped out before the vehicle had fully settled.","She hurried to the reception desk.","\"A fifteen-year-old boy was brought in from a residential school this morning,\" she said. \"He’s listed under the name Jae.\"","\"Are you listed as family or an emergency contact?\"","\"I’m his sister. Here’s my ID.\"","The nurse checked the computer again.","\"The school listed an old emergency contact. We’ve been trying to reach them for hours, but no one has answered.\"","Then she read it aloud.","Eira froze.","She knew that number.","It belonged to Alpha Sebastian."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230 The Boy Behind the Glass","paragraphs":["Eira did not wait for the elevator. She took the stairs two at a time, her boots striking the concrete until she reached the surgical floor.","She knew she could not get past the double doors marked SURGERY.","AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY.","Still, she kept walking until a nurse stopped her near the waiting area.","\"Ma’am, you need to stay behind the line.\"","\"I’m his sister.\"","\"I understand, but the surgical unit is restricted. Please wait here.\"","Eira stopped just outside the doors.","A few minutes later, Alpha Killian came around the corner. He had stayed at the emergency desk to get an update and make sure the hospital had the correct contact information.","No one could tell him much. Sam was in surgery, and the doctors would speak with the family when they had something definite to report.","Alpha Killian found Eira standing perfectly still among the other waiting families. She was not pacing or twisting her hands. She looked frozen.","Then he saw the tears running down her cheeks.","\"Eira.\" His voice was low. \"The nurse said the injury is to his leg. They found no obvious head trauma.\"","\"Killian.\" Her whisper broke. \"If I had come last night...\"","\"Don’t.\" He stepped in front of her. \"Even if you had come, the school would not have let you through that gate. You couldn’t have known what was happening inside.\"","\"This is Sebastian’s fault.\" Her voice shook. \"He buried that boy in a place like this, then couldn’t even be bothered to check on him.\"","Alpha Killian did not argue.","Eira wiped at her cheeks, but more tears followed.","He brushed one away with his thumb. Her skin was cold. Without a word, he took off his coat and draped it around her shoulders. The wool still held his warmth.","\"Listen to me.\" His voice stayed calm and firm. \"We wait for the surgeon. If this hospital can’t provide what Sam needs, we arrange a transfer. A trauma center, a children’s hospital, wherever the doctors recommend. Money and planes are not the problem.\"","The certainty in his voice finally broke through her fear.","\"Killian, I’m scared.\" She gripped the front of his shirt. \"I’m scared Sam won’t make it. I took Sebastian back to the orphanage. I gave Sam his number.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","\"You brought Sebastian back because you believed he was family. You gave Sam a way to contact him because you cared what happened to that boy.\" He lowered himself in front of her and rested his hands lightly on her knees. \"Sebastian abused that trust. He took Sam and abandoned him. That is on Sebastian. Not you.\"","Eira shook her head, crying silently.","\"This has nothing to do with who you love or who you try to help,\" Alpha Killian continued. \"It has to do with what Sebastian chose to do. Do you understand?\"","\"I hear you.\"","\"That’s not what I asked.\"","She looked down at him.","\"Do you understand that this is not your fault?\"","Eira pressed her lips together, then nodded.","Alpha Killian rose and wiped the last tear from her cheek.","Before he could say anything else, the hospital elevator opened.","The school’s principal arrived with the county liaison and two staff members. They approached in a rush, speaking over one another.","\"It was a tragic accident.\"","\"We’re prepared to discuss medical expenses.\"","\"The school has always followed safety procedures.\"","\"Please,\" Alpha Killian said.","His voice was quiet, but it cut through the hallway.","Everyone fell silent.","He turned toward the principal.","\"Not one more word about compensation or an accident until the surgeon tells us whether that boy will live.\"","The principal’s face went pale.","Alpha Killian stepped closer.","\"After that, you will provide every incident report, staffing record, camera log, and emergency call connected to Sam’s fall.\"","\"We cannot release confidential—\"","\"You can preserve them,\" Alpha Killian cut in. \"The county liaison is standing right there. If anything disappears before the investigation begins, your school will have a much bigger problem than a lawsuit.\"","The liaison’s expression hardened. \"He’s right. Do not alter or destroy anything.\"","The principal swallowed.","Behind the surgical doors, a red status light remained on.","Eira stared at it, wrapped in Alpha Killian’s coat, while the hallway fell silent around them.","Alpha Killian took out his phone and called Kate.","\"Book the first available flight to the county,\" he said. \"Bring Dr. Wood. Have our legal team contact the hospital and child protective services. No one discusses a settlement until the investigation is complete.\"","He ended the call, then returned with a cup of hot chocolate and placed it in Eira’s hands.","She wrapped her fingers around the warm cup. \"Thank you.\"","Before Alpha Killian could answer, the red light above the operating room went out.","A surgeon stepped through the doors and lowered his mask.","Eira rose so quickly that the chair scraped across the floor.","\"Doctor?\"","\"Are you Sam’s family?\"","\"I’m his sister.\"","The surgeon gave a brief nod. \"The surgery went well. Sam had a serious fracture in his leg, but the more urgent problem was bleeding inside his skull. We relieved the pressure and stabilized it. He’ll be moved to the ICU for close monitoring.\"","Eira’s knees weakened. She caught the back of the chair.","\"Is he out of danger?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"He’s stable for now,\" the surgeon said. \"The next twenty-four hours will be important.\"","Eira swallowed. \"You said there were other injuries.\"","The surgeon’s expression turned grave.","\"During the examination, we found extensive bruising across his body. Some of it appears recent. Some injuries may be older. We also found marks that are concerning for possible human bites, along with signs of fractures that may not have received proper medical treatment.\"","Eira went cold.","\"Bites?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"Marks consistent with possible bites,\" the surgeon clarified. \"We’ve documented everything and notified the hospital social worker. Because Sam is a minor and came from a residential program, the hospital is required to make a report to County Child Welfare. Law enforcement may also become involved.\"","\"He lives at the school,\" Alpha Killian said.","The surgeon held his gaze. \"Then the school will need to explain how those injuries happened. For now, the ICU team needs to keep him stable.\"","\"They will,\" Alpha Killian said.","A nurse led them to the ICU.","Sam lay beneath a thin blanket, his face pale against the white pillow. His injured leg was secured in a brace, and wires connected him to the monitors beside the bed. Bruises showed above the collar of his hospital gown.","Eira sat beside him, afraid to touch him. She watched the green line on the monitor rise and fall.","Alpha Killian stepped into the hall and made several calls.","When he returned, a nurse was standing beside the bed.","\"Sam will remain in the ICU until the doctors are satisfied that he’s stable,\" she said. \"After that, they’ll decide whether he can be moved to a private room.\"","Alpha Killian nodded. \"Understood.\"","Eira kept her eyes on Sam.","\"The surgeon documented the injuries,\" Alpha Killian said quietly. \"The hospital social worker has started the required reports.\"","\"The police,\" Eira whispered. \"I want them here.\"","\"They’ll be notified through the hospital’s report,\" Alpha Killian said. \"I’ll also make sure our attorney contacts the county investigators.\"","Eira finally looked at him. Her eyes were red, but her voice was steady.","\"I want to know who did this to him.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression hardened.","\"Then we’ll find out. We’ll do it properly, and whoever hurt Sam will answer for it.\""]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231 The Boy Who Flinched","paragraphs":["Sam finally stirred near dusk.","Eira rose at once and leaned over the bed. \"Sam? Hey, sweetheart. You’re awake.\"","An oxygen tube rested beneath his nose. He blinked up at her, dazed and frightened, as if he could not believe she was real.","Maybe her call had reached him last night. Maybe he had heard her voice before he passed out.","Alpha Killian reached toward the call button.","Sam’s eyes flew wide.","The monitor jumped into a rapid, uneven beep. His whole body tensed beneath the blanket.","Eira caught Alpha Killian’s wrist before he could touch the button and pulled his hand out of Sam’s sight.","\"Hey, it’s okay.\" She bent closer. \"You’re safe. No one is going to hurt you.\"","She released Alpha Killian and pressed the button herself.","A nurse arrived with the doctor a moment later. The instant Sam saw the white coat, panic took over again. His breathing quickened, and his hands began to shake.","Eira stepped between him and the doctor.","\"Give him some space.\"","The doctor stopped.","\"It’s okay, honey,\" Eira whispered. \"You don’t have to be scared. He’s just here to check on you.\"","Alpha Killian watched Sam’s reaction, then looked at the doctor.","\"Lose the coat,\" he said quietly. \"Come back without it.\"","The doctor stepped into the hall and returned a moment later in blue hospital scrubs. Eira kept hold of Sam’s hand while the nurse checked his vitals and the doctor completed a brief exam.","Sam stayed tense, but he no longer panicked.","\"Keep talking to him,\" the doctor told Eira. \"Your voice seems to calm him.\"","Alpha Killian nodded toward the hallway. \"Stay with him.\"","He followed the doctor outside.","Eira settled back into the chair and looked down at the hand she was holding.","Then she saw it.","Sam’s right thumb was missing from the first joint.","Her breath caught.","The surgeon’s words came back to her. The bruises. The old fractures. The possible bite marks. Sam’s terror when Alpha Killian reached for the call button. The way he had reacted to the doctor’s coat.","What had happened to him over the past two years?","What had the school done to him during the days he had been there?","Eira forced the questions down. Sam was awake, injured, and still afraid. She would not make him relive anything before he was ready.","Tears blurred her vision.","Then Sam’s fingers tightened around hers.","\"Sis,\" he whispered.","The word came out rough and dry.","Eira wiped her eyes and smiled. \"Yeah. I’m right here.\"","\"Sis.\"","Two years ago, the first time Sam had called her that, something inside her had changed. He had become her little brother in every way that mattered.","Now he gave her a weak, crooked smile. It was dazed and trusting, almost boyish.","Her chest ached.","Sam had not been the child she spent the most time with at Miss Gwen’s home. He was simply the one she had grown soft for, the one she had secretly given her number to.","But it would not have mattered which child had reached for her. Any child looking at her with that much fear and trust would have broken her heart.","She had a hundred questions.","Who hurt him? Why had he been sent away? Why had someone cut off his thumb? What had happened at the school?","But Sam was exhausted, medicated, and barely able to speak.","Eira squeezed his hand.","\"Rest now,\" she whispered. \"We’ll talk later.\"","She would wait until the police arrived.","--","Hale Tower was finally quiet.","Alpha Sebastian had just finished the launch ceremony for the Snowmark account. At least that deal was secure. The problems waiting behind it had not gone anywhere.","His annual report was due next. The Carter Group’s shareholder meeting was only days away, and despite securing the Snowmark contract, Alpha Sebastian had still lost the Sovereign Processor Initiative.","Alpha Sebastian could already picture the older board members sitting around the conference table, smiling politely as they picked apart his performance.","His report was thin. He had no major project to announce and no breakthrough to show for the year.","Alpha Carter would find a way to make it worse. Fiona always did.","Alpha Sebastian pressed two fingers to the bridge of his nose.","A knock sounded at the door.","\"Come in.\"","Beta Jordan stepped inside with a tablet in hand. \"Alpha, your phone has been off all day. Fiona’s office forwarded her call to me.\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced at the dead phone on his desk. Then he remembered the unknown number that had called again and again during the night.","\"I forgot to turn it back on.\" He picked up the phone. \"Isn’t Fiona at headquarters? What does she want?\"","\"The Omega Home and the other orphanages are being included in one combined donation drive this year. No special exceptions. The internal memo went out this morning.\"","Beta Jordan hesitated.","\"There’s more.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked up.","\"The trip lead has been reassigned. Finn is handling it this year. Alpha Carter said you don’t need to spend your time on that kind of work anymore.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened.","Beta Jordan did not need to spell it out. The Omega Home was where Eira had grown up. The Carter siblings knew exactly what they were doing.","The memo had already been distributed. Arguing now would only make him look defensive.","\"Understood.\"","Sebastian turned on his phone.","Notifications flooded the screen, but no new calls came through. He opened the call history.","The same unknown number appeared again and again.","More than twenty missed calls.","He tapped the number.","The area code was 530, somewhere in Northern California.","Sebastian froze.","That was where Sam had been moved.","Sam.","It had to be him.","He hit redial."]}]);
